WHAT THIS DIFF CONTAINS
  The L1+L2+L3 substrate (carried in from L3_T1_state.diff) PLUS L4's own changes:
  the three build fixes, the age-source census, the training-store stamps, the two retrained
  fitted artifacts and their field-level re-pins, and the fv re-pin the C.1 hazard forced.

WHAT IT DOES NOT CONTAIN — and why
  cm_400.pkl (band) · q97m.pkl · bust_prior_table.json are UNMOVED. Each has a measured reason
  recorded in L4_BUILD.md; none is an omission. The tree is unbakeable and nothing here has landed.

WHAT THIS DIFF CANNOT CARRY — stated so nobody reads it as "the full state"
  `git diff` covers TRACKED files only. The L4 run also produced two UNTRACKED tier-2 stamp files
  in the repo tree:

      engine/rl_after/peak_model_v4.pkl.srcmd5
      engine/rl_after/pvc_snapshot.json.srcmd5

  They are build products of the peak-model build (regenerated by re-running it), they are NOT
  committed, and they are NOT in this diff. The chain that exited 96 PASS / 1 FAIL had them present.

  This is the same shape as the omission that produced the whole v0surf episode: L1_amended_state.diff
  was described as capturing the tree "in full" and silently did not carry data/v0surf.pkl's bytes.
  A state diff captures tracked, changed files. It is not a container image. Reconstruct by applying
  this diff at the base AND re-running the build (31s) to regenerate the stamps.
